Bounded UART excerpt: real rc.unslung autostart guest run (Issue #81 / PR #86, 2026-11-16)
==========================================================================================

Provenance
----------
- Scenario: lab/scenarios/ported-mt7621-entware-autostart.json (59 steps)
- Tested source SHA: abf9f25 (PR #86 HEAD, CI green on that SHA; branch
  lab/mt7621-entware-autostart-20261115 from the combined candidate acb32ae)
- Driver:   lab/mt7621/entware_e2e.py run() path (fresh NAND copy, freshly
            built ext4 image, pinned 25-package mipselsf mirror per
            lab/entware-mipselsf.lock.json; private WSL/QEMU MT7621 stand,
            offline WAN, loopback-only forwards)
- Result:   PASS 59/59, 744.57 s, failure=None (report.json, same folder)
- UART:     private console log, 4593 lines, 3 full boot cycles
            ("Starting kernel" at console lines 31, 1809, 3226)
- The full UART log stays outside the repository; below are the only excerpted
  segments (console line numbers from that private log).
- What the run proves: KeeneticOS Ported actually EXECUTES the configured
  Entware init script (/opt/etc/init.d/rc.unslung) at boot — once per boot,
  right after the USB disk is mounted to /opt — and the S99labboot probe
  starts a live worker and increments a persistent boot-generation marker,
  with NO manual start anywhere.  This is process evidence, not the
  "configured init script" log line alone.

