3139: labboot-autostart gen=1 pid=701

(ndm applies the init-script setting at config time, but rc.unslung runs
~29 s AFTER "system ready", once the USB disk is mounted to /opt and
initialized; the probe's /dev/console echo lands immediately after the
mount.  The SSH proofs then confirmed: /proc/mounts "/opt ext4", the probe
still executable, "LABBOOT gen=1 pid=[0-9]+" from status, the generation
file exactly 1, a live sleep-3600 worker identified via /proc/<pid>/cmdline
and exactly one worker in /proc — report steps 34-43.  The marker wait
"labboot-autostart gen=1" (step 33) is part of the committed scenario.)

Segment 4 - boot 2 -> boot 3: QEMU monitor "system_reset" boundary (event 2)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
3205: Clocks: CPU: 880MHz, DDR: 1200MHz, Bus: 220MHz, Ref: 40MHz
3217: Booting image from flash bank 0 at 0x180000 ...
3226: Starting kernel at 0x813e3e44...
3230: Linux version 4.9-ndm-5 (t.me/project_athens)

(Scenario step 45 is the runner action "reset": run.py records the console
EOF offset BEFORE sending "system_reset" via the QEMU monitor, then sends
it.  Boot 3 is the post-reset cold start: NO init-shutdown lines and NO
"reboot: Restarting system" line appear between boot 2 and boot 3 — the
only native reboot line in the entire log is at console line 1777, so the
native reboot and the QEMU reset are two separate, individually observable
events.)

Segment 5 - boot 3: rc.unslung EXECUTES the probe again, generation 2
---------------------------------------------------------------------
4379: [I] Jan  1 03:04:05 ndm: Opkg::Manager: disk is set to: KASOPT:/.
4380: [I] Jan  1 03:04:05 ndm: Opkg::Manager: configured init script: "/opt/etc/init.d/rc.unslung".
4383: [I] Jan  1 03:04:05 ndm: Core::Server: system ready, core startup time is 95 seconds.
   ...[~160 lines of startup noise]...
4547: [I] Jan  1 03:04:31 ndm: Opkg::Manager: /tmp/mnt/11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555 mounted to /opt/.
4548: [I] Jan  1 03:04:31 ndm: Opkg::Manager: /tmp/mnt/11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555 initialized.
4549: [I] Jan  1 00:04:32 dropbear[694]: Running in background
4550: Got signal 1 to process...
4551: labboot-autostart gen=2 pid=702

(The persistent generation file survived the reset and the probe incremented
it 1 -> 2; the worker PID numeral changed 701 -> 702.  PID reuse across
reboots is legal, so the scenario records both numerals (PIDS step) but
never asserts equality/difference; the liveness proof is the
/proc/<pid>/cmdline identity, not the numeral.  The SSH proofs confirmed:
"/opt ext4", "LABBOOT gen=2 pid=[0-9]+", generation file exactly 2, live
worker identity, PIDS "701's value 702's value" recorded echo-safe, and
exactly one worker — report steps 53-59.)

MIPSEL_AUTOSTART derivation
---------------------------
python3 lab/mt7621/mt7621_gates.py --autostart-scenario
lab/scenarios/ported-mt7621-entware-autostart.json --autostart-report
<real report.json> derives:
  MIPSEL_AUTOSTART = PASS
  (native_reboot_then_qemu_reset_service_autostarted)
The gate requires the UART execution markers on both post-reboot boots, a
live worker identity per boot via /proc/<pid>/cmdline, the boot-generation
increments 1 then exactly 2, the pre-reboot negative state, one native
reboot wait plus one separate reset action, and report outcome PASS.  The
name is outside GATES/NATIVE_GATES (the 19 core gates stay unchanged) and
apply_labels refuses any --set for it, so a PASS can only come from a
validated scenario report.  No manual gate override was used.

Sanitization notes
------------------
- The dropbear child-connection lines quoting the guest-side forwarded
  address are kept only as console context; no credentials, no host paths,
  no firmware/NAND content appear here — every quoted line is guest console
  output plus provenance.
- Guest wall-clock shows "Jan 1 03:0x"/"00:0x" (no RTC in the emulated
  board), as in all prior cycles on this stand.
- junit.xml contains only action names and durations; report.json contains
  only step actions/outcomes/timings and the scenario name.
